    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-specimen-match-3> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "docs/media/diatom_frustule_phase_sep_comparison.png (generated output)" ;
        dcterms:description "3x4 synthesis figure: Pass 2 rows A-B (Stage 1/2 sims, bicontinuous mesh, negative control, SEM B1/B2) plus Pass 3 row C; no specimen margin view exists to compare with C3 — docs/media/diatom_frustule_phase_sep_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py at a69596cc, image/png, 1162913 B, 2775×2070 px, artifact_sha256 a9c947d7cead9aa4a0732db15d97ed3496cfd5451433cba2f7314b23cf1a6e47 (sha256 a9c947d7cead9aa4a0732db15d97ed3496cfd5451433cba2f7314b23cf1a6e47), spec_fingerprint a0656c1e84af378ca65d37247e04ce369aa44a7a1166c9de2688cf2ac0451d64" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 85/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "The Pass 2 SEM segmentation of the SHA-256-locked C. wailesii valve (139 foramina, d_1/a_1 = 0.690 vs 0.6757, |psi_6| = 0.764; 74 cribrum sub-pores) is unchanged and the comparison figure now has 12 panels with the SEM panels B1/B2 beside the new 3-stage composite (C1) and a one-foramen zoom with a 200 nm scale bar (C2) that can be read against the SEM cribrum tier; the C3 disc visually resembles radial costae striation. Deductions, and the reason this dimension falls: the vendored specimen shows the valve face at three magnifications and NO valve margin, so the entire costae remediation (R1) has no specimen to match — its only reference is the model's own isotropic null (-5); the 3-stage model gives 4.8 cribrum per foramen versus Sumper's 7-19 and 5.0 cribrella per cribrum versus 7, and the Pass 2 two-stage run still gives 2.04 cribrum per foramen (-3); at 12.5 nm/px the tertiary pores are 3.4-3.7 px wide so panel C2's cribrella are at the grid floor (-2); the GIF right panel still hard-codes '(139 foramina)' as a title string rather than the segmented count (-1). Net 87 -> 85." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/centrifugal_front_three_stage_reference.json L1–L82: specimen gap recorded: no margin / costae view in the vendored SEM; the A reference is the model's isotropic null (model_prediction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/centrifugal_front_three_stage_reference.json#L1-L82>",
            "models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L1261–L1261: GIF right-panel title hard-codes '(139 foramina)' instead of the segmented count <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L1261-L1261>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-specimen-match-3> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.85"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

